        {
          "title": "Intervals: Overlap and Sort-First Mental Model",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Overlap Test",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Interval = ==[start, end]==",
                "a and b overlap iff ==a.start <= b.end== **AND** ==b.start <= a.end==",
                "Touching endpoints `[1,2]`,`[2,3]`: the statement decides"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Problem",
                "[1,2],[2,3]",
                "Compare"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Merge",
                  "{green:overlap}",
                  "`<=`"
                ],
                [
                  "Meeting rooms",
                  "{red:no overlap}",
                  "`<`"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Sort First",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "Sort",
                    "sub": "O(n log n)",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Scan once",
                    "sub": "O(n)",
                    "ink": "green"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Compare with previous",
                    "sub": "or running end",
                    "ink": "purple"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Sorted by start: compare each interval only with the ==previous== (or running end)",
                "{red:Never} check all pairs: O(n²)",
                "==Sort== dominates; the scan adds only O(n)"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Pick the Key",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Goal",
                "Sort by"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Merge, insert, count rooms",
                  "**start**"
                ],
                [
                  "Maximize kept intervals",
                  "**end**"
                ]
              ],
              "highlightRow": 1
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Decide first",
              "text": "Settle the ==touching-endpoint rule== (`<=` or `<`) before writing any code."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Merge Intervals and Insert Interval",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 1,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Merge Intervals and Insert Interval",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Merge: Sort, Then Scan",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==Sort by start==, keep a result list",
                "If `cur.start <= last.end`: extend `last.end`",
                "Else: append `cur` as a new interval",
                "Sort dominates: O(n log n); scan is O(n)"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "python",
              "lines": [
                "iv = [[1,3],[2,6],[8,10],[15,18]]",
                "res = []",
                "for s, e in sorted(iv):",
                "    if res and s <= res[-1][1]:",
                "        res[-1][1] = max(res[-1][1], e)",
                "    else:",
                "        res.append([s, e])",
                "print(res)"
              ],
              "note": "sorted() leaves the caller's list alone"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "output",
              "lines": [
                "[[1, 6], [8, 10], [15, 18]]"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "max, not cur.end",
              "text": "Use `max(last.end, cur.end)`. A fully contained interval like [2,3] inside [1,6] must **not** shrink the end."
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Insert Interval (sorted input, O(n))",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "chain",
              "spec": {
                "steps": [
                  {
                    "text": "Before",
                    "note": "add while interval.end < new.start",
                    "ink": "green"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Merge",
                    "note": "while interval.start <= new.end: min of starts, max of ends",
                    "ink": "orange"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "After",
                    "note": "add the rest unchanged",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Common Bugs",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Sorting the input **in place** when the caller expects the original order",
                "Mutating `res[-1]` when it is an {red:alias} of the caller's inner list",
                "Using `cur.end` instead of `max`"
              ],
              "style": "cross",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "red"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Meeting Rooms with a Min-Heap",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 2,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Meeting Rooms with a Min-Heap",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Meeting Rooms I",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==Sort by start==, then compare neighbours",
                "Return {red:false} if `intervals[i].start < intervals[i-1].end`",
                "Touching ([1,2],[2,3]) is fine, so use `<`, not `<=`"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Meeting Rooms II: the Heap",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Sort by start; min-heap holds **end times** of rooms in use",
                "==Heap size = rooms needed==; answer = max size seen",
                "Pop on `<=` so a meeting starting as another ends reuses the room"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "chain",
              "spec": {
                "steps": [
                  {
                    "text": "Next meeting",
                    "note": "in start order",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "top <= start?",
                    "note": "pop: room freed",
                    "ink": "orange"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Push end",
                    "note": "room now busy",
                    "ink": "green"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Track max size",
                    "note": "= answer",
                    "ink": "purple"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Example and Cost",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "python",
              "lines": [
                "import heapq",
                "heap, best = [], 0",
                "for s, e in sorted([[0,30],[5,10],[15,20]]):",
                "    if heap and heap[0] <= s: heapq.heappop(heap)",
                "    heapq.heappush(heap, e)",
                "    best = max(best, len(heap))",
                "    print(sorted(heap))",
                "print(best)"
              ],
              "note": "15 pops 10, pushes 20"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "output",
              "lines": [
                "[30]",
                "[10, 30]",
                "[20, 30]",
                "2"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "O(n log n) time, O(n) space",
              "text": "Wrong counts come from **not sorting first** or heapifying ==starts== instead of ends."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Sweep Line with Events",
      "role": "outline",
