          "title": "Sweep Line with Events",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Events and Running Sum",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Each interval → =={start, +1}== and =={end, -1}==",
                "Sort by time; ==running sum== = concurrent intervals",
                "Answer = ==max running sum==, at the peak time",
                "Example: 0:+1, 5:+1, 10:-1, 15:+1, 20:-1, 30:-1 → peak 2"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "python",
              "lines": [
                "iv = [[0, 30], [5, 10], [15, 20]]",
                "ev = sorted(e for s, t in iv for e in ((s, 1), (t, -1)))",
                "cur = peak = 0",
                "for _, d in ev:",
                "    cur += d; peak = max(cur, peak)",
                "print(peak)"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "output",
              "lines": [
                "2"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Ties at Equal Time",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Touching ends",
                "Process first"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "No overlap ([1,2],[2,3])",
                  "{green:-1 then +1}"
                ],
                [
                  "Counts as overlap",
                  "{red:+1 then -1}"
                ]
              ],
              "frame": "dashed"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Python tuples sort `(t, -1)` before `(t, +1)`"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Two Pointers and Heap",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Sorted `starts[]` and `ends[]`: if start < end, advance start, ==count++==",
                "Else advance end, ==count--==",
                "Beats heap on simplicity; same ==O(n log n)==",
                "Extends to weights (+w/-w), coordinate compression, difference arrays"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Tie rule",
              "text": "Wrong tie order overcounts rooms: touching [1,2],[2,3] must give **1**"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Non-Overlapping Intervals by End Time",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 4,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Non-Overlapping Intervals by End Time",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Goal and Greedy",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==Min removals== = `n` - max kept intervals",
                "Sort by **END** ascending",
                "Keep if `start >= lastEnd`, then `lastEnd = end`",
                "Else count one removal"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "python",
              "lines": [
                "iv.sort(key=lambda x: x[1])",
                "last, cut = float('-inf'), 0",
                "for s, e in iv:",
                "    if s >= last: last = e",
                "    else: cut += 1"
              ],
              "note": "cut is the answer"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Why End Time",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Earliest finish leaves the ==most room== for later intervals",
                "Sort by start fails on `[[1,100],[2,3],[3,4]]`",
                "It keeps the long `[1,100]` and drops both short ones"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Variants",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Problem",
                "Keep test",
                "Answer"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Activity selection",
                  "`start >= lastEnd`",
                  "kept"
                ],
                [
                  "Burst balloons",
                  "`start > lastEnd` (touching overlaps)",
                  "kept = arrows"
                ],
                [
                  "By start order",
                  "on overlap drop larger end",
                  "`lastEnd = min(lastEnd, end)`"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Init and cost",
              "text": "Start `lastEnd` at ==-infinity==, not 0: starts can be negative. Time **O(n log n)**, extra space **O(1)**."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
